>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dirks</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Visualizing telomere dynamics in living mammalian cells using PNA probes</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>6631</fpage><lpage>6641</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14657034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gorisch</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lichter</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rippe</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mobility of multi-subunit complexes in the nucleus: accessibility and dynamics of chromatin subcompartments</article-title><source>Histochem Cell Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>123</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>228</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15830242</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lanctot</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheutin</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Cremer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Cavalli</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Cremer</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dynamic genome architecture in the nuclear space: regulation of gene expression in three dimensions</article-title><source>Nat Rev Genet</source><year>2007</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>115</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17230197</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cabal</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name><name><surname>Genovesio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodriguez-Navarro</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zimmer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gadal</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Lesne</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Buc</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Feuerbach-Fournier</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Olivo-Marine</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurt</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Nehrbass</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>SAGA interacting factors confine sub-diffusion of transcribed genes to the nuclear envelope</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2006</year><volume>441</volume><fpage>770</fpage><lpage>773</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16760982</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chubb</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyle</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Perry</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bickmore</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chromatin motion is constrained by association with nuclear compartments in human cells</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>439</fpage><lpage>445</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11909528</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Handwerger</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gall</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Steady-state dynamics of Cajal body components in the <italic>Xenopus </italic>germinal vesicle</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>160</volume><fpage>495</